= Computer security — Simple =

'''Computer security''' is protecting computers, networks, software, and information from unwanted access, changes, leaks, damage, or interruption.

Security can mean keeping information secret, making sure data is not changed improperly, and keeping services available.

It also includes checking identity and controlling what people or programs are allowed to do.

Security is not only encryption.

Passwords, permissions, updates, backups, monitoring, hardware protections, and safe system design can all matter.

No computer system is simply “secure” against everything. A useful security claim says what threats it is designed to resist.

